# Clockspeed - .gitignore
#
# This file lands BEFORE the first commit. See BOOTSTRAP.md section 8.1 ("Add these to
# .gitignore before the first commit"), section 12 non-negotiables 2 and 3, and
# CONVENTIONS.md section 17 ("From day one, even while private").
#
# Three classes of thing are excluded here and each is excluded for a different reason.
# The reason is stated on every group. If you are about to add a pattern, say which of
# the three it is:
#
#   PUBLISHER-OWNED  - game data and anything extracted from the game install. Not ours
#                      to redistribute. Read it from the local install at runtime.
#   PII-BEARING      - carries the operator's identity. Save headers embed the platform
#                      name, a platform account id and the player's display name as
#                      plaintext hex (BOOTSTRAP section 2.2). A leak here is permanent
#                      once it is in git history.
#   LOCAL-ONLY       - machine-specific wiring, secrets, generated caches and runtime
#                      state. Never the same on two machines, so tracking it is drift.
#
# A pattern with a leading slash is anchored to the repo root. That anchoring is
# load-bearing: /data/ is the generated-artifact directory and MUST NOT touch the
# clockspeed/data/ SOURCE package. Do not remove a leading slash without checking.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEGATION TEST - these paths MUST stay tracked.
#
# After editing this file, run:
#     git check-ignore -v config/ports.json .claude/settings.json .githooks/pre-commit
# and repeat for each path below. Every one of them MUST report NO match. If any path
# below is reported as ignored, this file has a bug: narrow the offending pattern.
# Do NOT paper over it with a wider negation - a negation that re-includes a directory
# can re-include a secret that a later pattern was meant to catch.
#
#   config/ports.json
#   .claude/settings.json
#   .claude/agents/planner.md
#   .claude/commands/done.md
#   .github/workflows/tier1.yml
#   .githooks/pre-commit
#   tools/drift_guard.py
#   scripts/verify_env.py
#   tests/test_ratio.py
#   docs/LEDGER.md
#   docs/adr/README.md
#   clockspeed/data/registry.py
#   clockspeed/save/usmap.py
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ===========================================================================
# PUBLISHER-OWNED - game data and anything extracted from the game install.
# Never commit these. Not a slice, not a sample, not "just one small fixture".
# Test fixtures are small synthetic registries hand-authored in the repo
# (BOOTSTRAP section 8.1), never cuts of real game data.
# ===========================================================================

# Unreal packaged content and property mappings
*.pak
*.ucas
*.utoc
*.usmap
*.uasset
*.uexp
*.umap

# First-party reference material shipped in the install's CommunityResources
Headers.zip
CustomVersions.json
DedicatedServerAPIDocs.md
FactoryGame.usmap

# Locale documentation dumps. The English one alone is over 10 MB and there are
# dozens of siblings. Matched by FILENAME SHAPE, because a locale dump dropped
# anywhere in the tree is the accident being prevented.
#
# The shapes are the real ones on disk: xx.json (io), xx-XX.json (en-US),
# xx-NNN.json (es-419), xx-Xxxx.json (zh-Hans).
#
# Deliberately NOT written as Docs/*.json: git matches ignore patterns
# case-insensitively when core.ignorecase is set, which it is on Windows, so
# Docs/ would also silently swallow docs/ - and docs/ must stay tracked.
#
# Cost of these patterns: a two-letter tracked .json basename would be ignored.
# There is none, and if one is ever needed, rename it - this shape is spoken for.
??.json
??-??.json
??-???.json
??-????.json
en-US.json

# Any local staging or scratch copy of install content
/gamedata/
/CommunityResources/
/game/


# ===========================================================================
# PII-BEARING - save files and everything derived from them.
# A .sav embeds the platform account id and the player display name in plain
# hex inside the header options string (BOOTSTRAP section 2.2, measured).
# A save file is a personal-data-bearing artifact: never commit one, never
# attach one to an issue, never place one in a fixture directory.
# ===========================================================================

*.sav
*.sav.bak
*.savbackup

# Snapshot corpus of the pinned reference world as it grows
# (BOOTSTRAP section 2.3 - "Snapshot copies at milestones into a gitignored
# corpus directory"). Regression input, permanently local.
/corpus/

# Save copies made for parsing. The game holds handles during autosave, so the
# reader copies out before parsing (BOOTSTRAP section 8.2). Those copies are
# still real saves and still carry PII.
/work/

# Screen and HUD capture artifacts (CONVENTIONS.md section 17: gitignore every
# capture artifact). A screenshot of the game shows the world and the player.
/captures/
/screenshots/


# ===========================================================================
# LOCAL-ONLY - generated artifacts.
# ===========================================================================

# The generated artifact directory (BOOTSTRAP section 6: "data/  generated
# artifacts - GITIGNORED"). Anchored, so clockspeed/data/ source is untouched.
/data/

# The advice ledger and the global per-rule mutes (BOOTSTRAP section 5.2:
# "a plain JSON file in the project data directory ... It is gitignored").
# Per-world advice state. Regenerable, machine-local, and it names worlds.
/data/ledger.json
/data/mutes.json
*.ledger.json


# ===========================================================================
# LOCAL-ONLY - configuration and wiring that is per machine.
# These name interpreters, absolute home paths and account directories, which
# CONVENTIONS.md section 10 forbids in a tracked file.
# ===========================================================================

.mcp.json
.claude/settings.local.json
*.local.json
config/local.json
.env
.env.*

# Agent worktrees. Session 3 measured why this line is not optional: with the
# directory untracked but UNIGNORED, `git status` reported it as a candidate for
# commit - so one `git add -A` would have committed a full duplicate of the tree,
# including whatever half-finished state a builder was mid-edit on. It also
# silently widened the local lint surface, because ruff respects .gitignore and
# nothing else was excluding it: `ruff format --check .` went from 38 files to
# 187 and reported a "failure" that was really a builder's scratch copy. The
# main tree was clean the whole time. CI never saw either problem - a fresh
# checkout has no worktrees - which is exactly what makes it a local-only false
# red, and a gate the operator learns to distrust.
/.claude/worktrees/

# Local semantic recall store. Markdown in memory/ is the source of truth; the
# store is a mirror and is rebuilt by tools/memory_sync.py (CONVENTIONS.md
# section 11.2 - "The store, its config and its wiring are LOCAL and gitignored").
/.recall/
/memory/*.db
/memory/*.sqlite
/memory/*.sqlite3


# ===========================================================================
# LOCAL-ONLY - certificates and keys.
# The dashboard's self-signed certificate is generated by a tracked script into
# a gitignored location (BOOTSTRAP section 7.1). The script is the artifact;
# the key never is.
# ===========================================================================

/certs/
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cer
*.der
*.pfx
*.p12


# ===========================================================================
# LOCAL-ONLY - generated caches and build output.
# ===========================================================================

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.tox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
/build/
/dist/
.venv/
venv/

# Node exists solely for the Electron shell (BOOTSTRAP section 11).
node_modules/
shell/dist/
# Written by the tier-2 shell job so the TAP trailer can be parsed after the
# exit code is captured. Ephemeral in CI; litter when the step is run by hand.
shell/tap.txt
shell/out/
# Written by the NVIDIA user-mode driver, not by anything in this project, when
# Electron is launched with `shell/` as its working directory - which is exactly
# how the desktop shortcut launches it. The directory arrives empty, so it is
# invisible to git today; the entry is here for the day the driver puts a log in
# it. tests/shell/test_shell_assets.py enumerates this subtree with `--others
# --exclude-standard`, so an un-ignored binary dropped here would redden the
# ASCII and carriage-return arms against a file nobody in this project authored.
# NARROW ON PURPOSE: this one vendor directory, not a wildcard over shell/.
shell/NVIDIA Corporation/


# ===========================================================================
# LOCAL-ONLY - runtime state.
# Live process state, PID files and logs. Logs quote parsed data and can echo
# header bytes, so they are treated as potentially PII-bearing too.
# ===========================================================================

/run/
/logs/
/var/
*.log

# The headless lane's control plane and its reports (CS-918). LOCAL-ONLY runtime
# state: the lane LOCK carries a live pid, a worktree path and a run id; the
# stop sentinels are operator gestures made on one machine; the reports hold
# per-cycle worker logs and the JSONL ledger. None of it is the same on two
# machines, and the worker logs quote whatever the worker printed - which can
# include a parsed save header - so they are treated as potentially PII-bearing
# like every other log here.
#
# The DIRECTORIES are ignored, not their contents, so nothing under them can be
# added by a `git add -A` that reaches inside. ops/loop/*.py and
# ops/loop/*.ps1 stay tracked: only these two subdirectories are runtime.
/ops/loop/control/
/ops/loop/reports/

# The lane's model config, read by ops/loop/run_lane.ps1 via $PSScriptRoot with
# a known-good fallback so a lane never fails to spawn over a config read.
# LOCAL-ONLY: which model a box drives its lane with is a machine choice, and
# tracking it would make one operator's pick everyone's.
/ops/loop/config.json

# The cross-project message channel. Sibling projects on this box drop notes
# here under a shared directory name, and every tree that uses it gitignores it.
# LOCAL-ONLY: a mailbox is machine-local by construction - what lands in it
# depends on which siblings exist beside this checkout, so it is never the same
# on two machines.
#
# It is ALSO treated as potentially PII-BEARING, like the logs above, and that
# is measured rather than assumed: the first note delivered here named a world
# discovered on this machine, as a whole word, in two places. The pre-commit
# gate blocked it under non-negotiable 3 when a `git add -A` swept the directory
# in. Notes here are authored by OTHER projects, which do not run this repo's
# redaction rules, so the next note is no safer than that one was.
#
# The DIRECTORY is ignored, not its contents, so nothing inside it can be added
# by a `git add -A` that reaches in.
#
# ANCHORED on purpose: the channel is a root-level convention in every tree that
# uses it. A copy at any other depth is unexpected, and should stay visible to
# `git status` and be blocked by the gate rather than silently ignored - the
# diagnosable fail-closed this repo's PII surfaces choose everywhere else.
/moon_sync_inbox/

# CS-1161. THE OUTBOX, on the same terms and anchored the same way. It was
# missing until 2026-09-20, so the half of the channel this tree AUTHORS was
# the unprotected half: `git check-ignore -q moon_sync_inbox` exited 0 and the
# outbox exited 1, while `git status` reported `?? moon_sync_outbox/` holding
# three delivered notes. A sibling filed the anticipatory version of this
# against an EMPTY directory of its own the day before; this tree was already
# past that point. Correspondence between checkouts on one machine is not
# project history, and phase 7 is a public flip.
/moon_sync_outbox/


# ===========================================================================
# LOCAL-ONLY - OS and editor noise.
# ===========================================================================

Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/

# Playwright MCP scratch output. The audit browser writes screenshots and
# accessibility snapshots into the repo root; they are artifacts of a run, never
# content, and one reached a commit through `git add -A` before this line existed.
/.playwright-mcp/

# Session scratch under docs/. Working notes a slice needs while it runs -
# a classification table, a spec draft - that must never become a tracked doc
# and must never enter the doc-topology ownership table.
docs/_scratch/
